  "id": "COMPOUND:42654 - PROTEIN:4978",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 13-cis-Retinol and C8166 through a series of target interactions. 13-cis-Retinol is directly linked to the Potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including Caryophylla-2(12),6-dien-5-one and Labradorin 1. Both of these compounds are implicated in targeting C8166, indicating a possible pathway where 13-cis-Retinol influences the activity of the Potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which in turn affects C8166. The scores from the three paths are consistent, suggesting a reliable relationship. The evidence supports a mechanistic link where 13-cis-Retinol may modulate the function of the Potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which is a key player in the regulation of C8166. The presence of multiple targets and the similar scores across different paths indicate a robust and well-supported relationship.",
